== Relationships to other products

[TIP]
====
Record how this product relates to the others in the solution by linking it with the link symbol in the top level tool bar. Always link *from the part to the whole*: open the component and link it to the product it belongs to. Each relationship is then entered once, and the other product shows it from its own side automatically.

Choose the link type that matches how this product relates to the other one:

* *default component of* — it ships as a built-in part of the other product, not as a distinct product
* *external component of* — the other product needs it as an external dependency or library
* *installed on* — it runs on top of the other product, such as an operating system or hardware platform
* *installed with* — it is bundled and installed alongside the other product during setup
* *optional component of* — it is an add-on, plug-in or licensed extra for the other product

These are the relationship categories defined by the CSAF standard, so the security advisories and the SBOM can be generated from them directly.
