== Where this product appears in the threat model

[TIP]
====
Link this product to the elements of the threat model that it implements: the processes, data stores and trust boundaries that it is the software or hardware behind.

The easiest way is from the element itself, where the products that implement it are listed together with buttons for adding one. You can also do it from here, with the link symbol in the top level tool bar: choose *implements* and pick the element.

The link is what makes impact analysis possible. When a vulnerability is reported against this product, it is what tells you which parts of the system are affected and which interfaces are exposed.
